The generator keeps a fixed‑size list (or deque) that stores the most recent n items. As each new element is received, it replaces the oldest entry and, once the buffer is full, yields the current tuple of the last n elements. If the input iterable ends before the buffer reaches size n, the generator simply stops without producing any output.

