The function first normalizes each interval so that the start is the smaller value and the end is the larger one. It then computes the potential overlap by taking the maximum of the two starts and the minimum of the two ends. If the computed start is less than or equal to the computed end, the intervals overlap and the function returns the resulting interval; otherwise it returns None. This handles cases where one interval is completely inside the other, where they only touch at a point, and where they are disjoint.

