I will implement `retryAsync` by invoking the provided function `fn` repeatedly up to `attempts` times. Each call is awaited, and if it resolves, the promise resolves with that value. If it rejects, I capture the error and try again unless the maximum attempts have been reached, in which case the final error is thrown. This approach avoids any sleeping between retries, as requested.

