js-021.text:
I will create a function `once` that wraps the given function `fn`. The wrapper will keep track of whether `fn` has been called before using a flag. On the first call, it will execute `fn`, store the result, and set the flag to true. Subsequent calls will simply return the stored result without invoking `fn` again. This approach handles edge cases such as `fn` throwing an error on the first call (the error will be thrown each time) and ensures the result is cached after the first successful execution.

ANSWER:
