```

js-038.text:
I'll create a throttle function that only executes the provided function when the tick method has been called since the last execution. The first call will always run regardless of tick state. I need to track the last execution time and ensure the function only runs when tick has been invoked after the previous execution.

ANSWER:
```javascript
function throttleManual(fn) {
  let lastExecution = 0;
  let hasTicked = false;

  const call = () => {
    if (hasTicked) {
      fn();
      lastExecution = Date.now();
      hasTicked = false;
    }
  };

  const tick = () => {
    hasTicked = true;
  };

  return { call, tick };
}

module.exports = throttleManual;
```

