js-044.text:
I will implement `formatBytes` by checking the magnitude of the input number against powers of 1024, selecting the appropriate unit (B, KB, MB, …), and formatting the value with one decimal place when necessary. The function will treat values less than 1024 as bytes, round to one decimal for larger units, and handle zero and negative numbers gracefully.

ANSWER:
module.exports = function formatBytes(n) {
  if (n === 0) return '0 B';
  const units = ['B', 'KB', 'MB', 'GB', 'TB'];
  const k = 1024;
  let i = 0;
  while (n >= k && i < units.length - 1) {
    n /= k;
    i++;
  }
  return n % 1 === 0 ? `${n} ${units[i]}` : `${n.toFixed(1)} ${units[i]}`;
};

